Ladybird masks VENDOR, RENDERER, VERSION, and SHADING_LANGUAGE_VERSION
per navigator compatibility mode and shapes the unmasked pair likewise.
Blink’s WebGLRenderingContextBase::getParameter() answers “WebKit”,
“WebKit WebGL”, “WebGL 1.0 (” + the driver’s version + “)”, and
“WebGL GLSL ES 1.0 (” + the driver’s GLSL version + “)”, with the
WebGL 2 context substituting 2.0 and 3.00; through the command buffer
the driver strings read “OpenGL ES 2.0 Chromium” and
“OpenGL ES GLSL ES 1.0 Chromium”. WebKit’s answers are “WebKit”,
“WebKit WebGL”, “WebGL 1.0”, and “WebGL GLSL ES 1.0 (1.0)” (3.00 for
WebGL 2), and on Apple platforms its unmasked pair is “Apple Inc.” and
“Apple GPU”. Gecko’s ClientWebGLContext::GetParameter() answers
“Mozilla” for VENDOR and the sanitized renderer for RENDERER;
webgl::SanitizeRenderer() maps any Apple GPU to “Apple M1” and appends
“, or similar”, and SanitizeVendor() reduces the vendor to its bare
name (“Apple”, “NVIDIA Corporation”, “Intel”, “AMD”). Ladybird copies
the Apple rule and the vendor table; other GPUs keep their own
renderer string with the “, or similar” marker, where Gecko has a
table of representative devices.
